      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Host-guest control can use a vsock channel without consuming ordinary host TCP endpoints. Internet access is a separate path. Enforce destination policy outside the untrusted guest: block metadata and internal destinations, validate resolved addresses, and recheck redirects and connection targets. A domain allowlist alone can miss a changed DNS answer.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 24.136,
          "duration": 23.736,
          "until": 24.785999999999998
        },
        {
          "say": "A credential broker can expose an opaque reference while keeping the real secret outside the guest. The reference still grants scoped authority, so bind it to job, destination, method, and permitted operation. Inject credentials only on an approved connection. Bound output, network volume, time, and retries, and preserve a restricted audit record.",
          "start": 24.785999999999998,
          "end": 47.658,
          "duration": 22.872,
          "until": 48.30799999999999
        }
      ],
